    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "The product of two consecutive odd numbers is 195. Find the numbers.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$13$ and $15$, or $-15$ and $-13$.",
      "worked": "Let the consecutive odd numbers be $x$ and $x+2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x(x+2)&=195\\\\x^2+2x-195&=0\\\\(x+15)(x-13)&=0\\\\x&=-15\\text{ or }13.\\end{align*}$$\nThe numbers are $-15$ and $-13$, or $13$ and $15$. Both pairs consist of consecutive odd numbers and have product $195$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
